2. Current PostGIS Query and Indexes

Query (AreaRepository.findActiveInViewport):
SELECT * FROM area
WHERE workspace_id = :workspaceId
  AND status = 'ACTIVE'
  AND ST_Intersects(geometry, ST_MakeEnvelope(:minLon, :minLat, :maxLon, :maxLat, 4326))

Indexes (V2__core_schema.sql):
-- B-tree: pre-filters to one workspace before spatial work
CREATE INDEX idx_area_workspace_id ON area (workspace_id);

-- Partial GiST: covers only ACTIVE areas, the exact population the query reads
CREATE INDEX idx_area_active_geometry ON area USING GIST (geometry)
WHERE status = 'ACTIVE';

Query execution plan behavior: PostgreSQL uses idx_area_workspace_id to restrict to one workspace's rows, then idx_area_active_geometry for the bounding-box acceleration pass (GiST R-tree intersection), then an exact ST_Intersects check on the remaining candidates. For 10,000 polygons in a small geographic region, GiST reduces the exact-check candidate set to the tens-to-hundreds range.

Spatial semantics: ST_Intersects is exact — it returns an area if any part of its geometry touches the query envelope, including areas that only partially cross the viewport edge.

