8. Additional Alternative: Workspace Generation Counter

A simpler key design for workspace-wide invalidation without iterating the cache:

TileKey(workspaceId, generationId, z, x, y)

A ConcurrentHashMap<UUID, AtomicLong> workspaceGenerations maps each workspace to its current generation number. On any mutation in workspace W: generationId = workspaceGenerations.get(W).incrementAndGet(). Old entries become permanently unreachable (different key) and are evicted by Caffeine's size/TTL bounds.

Pros: Eviction is O(1) — just increment a counter. No cache iteration.
Cons: Stale entries consume memory until Caffeine evicts them by size/TTL. Slightly more complex to reason about.

For the prototype with a single workspace and modest cache size, simple cache.invalidateAll() on mutation is equivalent and simpler. The generation counter is worth considering for multi-workspace production.

